| Cross binutils | as, ld, ar, objdump, nm, strip, ranlib, windres, dlltool, dllwrap, addr2line, strings, readelf, size, elfedit, gprof + gcc-ar/gcc-nm/gcc-ranlib | Per K line 39. |
| winpthreads | `libpthread.a`, `libwinpthread.a`, `include/pthread.h` | Per K lines 60-66. |
| 32-bit cross | `/usr/bin/i686-w64-mingw32-gcc` is absent | Per K line 35. |
| lld absent | `/usr/bin/lld` is absent | Per K line 18. |
| xwin absent | `/usr/bin/xwin` is absent | Per K line 19. |

This anchor re-reads K's report. It does not re-stat, re-run, or re-verify any of the binary paths (the K sub-agent did the per-path read in its own session, lines 28-72). Trust chain: orchestrator's `dnf install` + `rpm -q` at survey time → K's per-path read → this anchor's re-read of K. The K report is dated 2026-08-19 (line 4). No decay within the day is plausible. The toolchain facts hold.

If the user later wants a fresh `dnf list installed` or a re-run of `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc --version`, that is a sub-agent K re-run, not a re-anchor.

